# Veycraft — Devin Desktop & Windsurf

Read [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md) and [skills/REGISTRY.md](./skills/REGISTRY.md) first; route natural-language requests via `skills/REGISTRY.md` without forcing `/setup` for standalone tasks, and load only the active skill bodies needed.

This is a **Markdown-first career operations repository with a zero-dependency Node.js CLI (`bin/cli.mjs`)** and optional Playwright/Notion MCP (compatible with Cognition Devin Desktop / ACP and legacy Windsurf):
- `/demo` -> `.agent/workflows/demo.md` (15-second synthetic sandbox; no personal data or browser login)
- `/quick-tailor` -> `.agent/workflows/quick-tailor.md` (1 real CV + 1 JD; no browser login)
- `/setup` or "Check my folder" -> `skills/00-interrogate-and-onboard.md` + `skills/01-resume-ingestion.md`
- `/daily-run` or `/apply-url <url>` -> `skills/00-daily-run.md`
- `/tailor-cv <url>` -> `skills/03-tailor-resume-and-verify.md`
- `/weekly-report` -> `skills/06-log-and-insights.md`
- `/linkedin-growth` -> `skills/linkedin-growth.md` + `skills/05-outreach-and-interview-prep.md`

See `adapters/apps/devin-desktop.md` for Devin Desktop / ACP MCP wiring (`mcp/mcp.template.json`). Local JSON under `logs/` is primary. Respect dry run, verified facts, caps, and explicit approval gates.
